bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_f64_option_inline_pass_compile_cost_on_option_dense_input_2026-11-28, 0, "The typed f64? inline-layout pass (src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/mir/float_option_inline.rs, run from lower_module) costs compile time and peak RSS on option-dense input. Measured aarch64, 4 alternated rounds, base seed dc41771399af764f vs dd4adb4888424f68: simple compile of a generated 39003-line file with 3000 functions that each hold two f64? locals (Some, copy, if val, ??) takes 1.103 s / 320 MB instead of 1.058 s / 280 MB (+4.3% time, +14% peak RSS), over the 2% budget. Ordinary code is flat (sfnt_glyf.spl 0.33 s vs 0.33 s, web_render_api.spl and webp_vp8_decode.spl within noise; a float loop with no option 4.680 s vs 4.735 s) because a function with no f64? local leaves the pass after one scan of its locals. An F64OPT timer put the pass itself at about 64 ms of the 3000 functions (about 21 us per function) before two rounds of tuning; with the kill switch the same binary compiles the file in 1.03-1.05 s / 288 MB. Likely causes: (a) time: for a function with a candidate the pass walks every instruction three to four times and calls MirInst::defs() / uses() on each, and both return a freshly allocated Vec (main scan, escape scan, touching scan, dead-producer scan); pair_local / payload_of / hidden / addrs are SipHash HashMaps. (b) RSS: the MIR really is larger - one Load of the one-word slot becomes two Loads (three instructions with the per-block LocalAddr), one Store becomes const + two Stores, each rt_is_some becomes const, BitAnd, const, compare - and every rewritten block is rebuilt in a second Vec<MirInst> while the old one is alive. Fix ideas: add allocation-free visitors MirInst::for_each_use / for_each_def and use them in the scans; fold the escape scan and the touching scan into the main scan by recording the instructions that mention a LocalAddr vreg of a candidate; key the remaining maps by dense vreg index like def_kind; emit presence as one compare against a hoisted zero (store the tag as 0 / non-zero so no BitAnd is needed, keeping the sub-kind in a separate slot only for locals that have a word); rewrite blocks in place when the instruction count does not grow."

